## Adjudication firewall

- `UNIQUE-COMMON-LAW` means one member of this frozen conditional H1 family
  survives the exact H2 source, state, and ordered-history gates.  It is not
  automatically an axiom derivation, arbitrary history, retained theory, or
  TOE closure.
- `PLURAL-SURVIVAL` means H2 does not select among multiple physically
  inequivalent survivors.  It does not by itself justify an axiom addition;
  generated histories, rate/action, and further held-outs remain live.
- `NO-MEMBER` rejects only this exact frozen H1 family on H2.  It is not a
  no-go for other local actions, larger condition alphabets, different
  source maps, other detector families, generated substrates, or the minimal
  axioms.  Any shipped negative must obey the current N1--N8 no-go discipline.

